text: "<!--\nThe output format. Every virality run ends in one file shaped like this, saved to\n./virality/<slug>/script.md and printed in chat. Rules:\n- SAY is spoken, SCREEN is the on-screen text (6 words or fewer), VISUAL is what the viewer sees.\n  List shots inside VISUAL with \" / \". No shot holds longer than about 1.5 seconds.\n- Timings come from `python3 tools/speech.py --line \"...\" --wpm <your pace>`, not guesses.\n- The hook leads with the payoff (money made or saved, or a number) in SAY or SCREEN.\n- One CTA: comment a one-word keyword, said out loud AND on screen, plus what they get.\n- Unknown numbers stay as {{your number}} and are flagged. Never invent one.\n- Keep on-screen text inside the Reels safe zone (1080x1920): y 240 to 1470, nothing on the\n  right rail (x > 950) below y 1000.\nThe worked example below is a fictional creator with illustrative numbers.\n-->\n# Script: The $62 grocery week\n\n- platform: Reels, TikTok, Shorts\n- length: 27.5s at 190 wpm (pace measured with speech.py)\n- formula: The Payoff (hookscore 80.8 STRONG, payoff LEADS at word 3)\n- keyword: PLAN\n- based on: @budgetbites, 1.2M views, 24x their own median (rewritten for this creator's audience)\n\n## Hook options (hookscore.py)\n\n| score | formula | spoken | on screen |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 80.8 STRONG | The Payoff | I feed four people on $62 a week. | $62 A WEEK. FAMILY OF 4. |\n| 62.6 OK | Unclassified | Three dinners under $2 a plate. | 3 DINNERS UNDER $2 |\n| 47.6 WEAK | Unclassified | Meal prep took my whole Sunday. Now: 40 minutes. | SUNDAY -> 40 MIN |\n\n## Script\n\n### 1. HOOK (0:00-0:03.2)\nSAY: I feed four people on $62 a week.\nSCREEN: $62 A WEEK. FAMILY OF 4.\nVISUAL: Face, bottom half / the real receipt slides in above, total circled in red\n\n### 2. PROOF (0:03.2-0:07.9)\nSAY: That's the receipt from Saturday. Every dinner this week came out of that one bag.\nSCREEN: THE ACTUAL RECEIPT\nVISUAL: Receipt full frame / pull back to the bag on the counter / five dinners laid out\n\n### 3. STEP ONE (0:07.9-0:12.9)\nSAY: First, I shop for three proteins, not seven. Chicken thighs, eggs, and a bag of lentils.\nSCREEN: 3 PROTEINS, NOT 7\nVISUAL: Hand drops thighs in cart / eggs / lentils / price tags close up\n\n### 4. STEP TWO (0:12.9-0:17.4)\nSAY: Then one Sunday cook. Forty minutes, two trays, and the oven does the work.\nSCREEN: 40 MINUTES. 2 TRAYS.\nVISUAL: Timer at 40:00 / trays going in / timer at 0:00 / trays out\n\n### 5. REHOOK (0:17.4-0:22.4)\nSAY: Here's the part nobody does. I write the week's dinners on the fridge before I shop.\nSCREEN: PLAN BEFORE YOU SHOP\nVISUAL: Marker on the fridge whiteboard / the five dinner names / face reacts\n\n### 6. CTA (0:22.4-0:27.5)\nSAY: Comment PLAN and I'll send you my exact $62 list and the five recipes.\nSCREEN: Comment \"PLAN\"\nVISUAL: Face full frame / keyword on the seam / list PDF thumbnail beside the head\n\n## Caption\n\nComment PLAN and I'll send you the $62 list and all five recipes.\n\nThree proteins, one Sunday cook, dinners on the fridge before the shop. That's the whole system for budget meal prep for a family of four.\n\n## Hashtags\n\n#mealprep #budgetmeals #familydinner\n\n## Cover\n\nCOVER: $62 A WEEK\nTITLE: How I feed a family of four for $62 a week\n\n## LinkedIn post (secondary)\n\nWe spent $250 a week on groceries. Now it's $62.\n\nThree changes did it. Three proteins instead of seven. One 40-minute Sunday cook. And the week's dinners written on the fridge before anyone goes to the shop.\n\nThe last one matters most. A plan turns a $250 wander into a $62 list.\n\nWhat is the one line on your shopping list you would never cut?\n"
